## Review
- Blocker: The Rust interaction lease is acquired only after the gesture crosses the drag threshold, leaving a race where pointer capture is already active but the transparent overlay remains eligible for click-through. `attachPetPointerDrag` captures the pointer on `pointerdown` without notifying Rust ([windows/src/pet-pointer-drag.ts:43](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/pet-pointer-drag.ts:43)-[56](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/pet-pointer-drag.ts:56)); `WindowDragController` calls the host start hook only after `movedBeyondThreshold` ([windows/src/window-drag.ts:63](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/window-drag.ts:63)-[70](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/window-drag.ts:70)); and the hook is where `set_pet_dragging(true)` is awaited ([windows/src/pet-window.ts:340](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/pet-window.ts:340)-[347](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/pet-window.ts:347)). Meanwhile the 60ms native loop sets `ignore_cursor_events(true)` whenever the cursor is outside the hit rectangle and no active lease exists ([windows/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:683](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:683)-[687](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:687), [windows/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:745](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:745)-[750](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:750)). A fast pointer movement out of the sprite/bubble can therefore be made click-through before the asynchronous lease request completes, which can prevent the captured webview from receiving `pointerup`/`pointercancel` and leave the gesture unfinished. Acquire the lease at accepted `pointerdown` (release it for click/cancel and after final drag completion), or make the native loop honor an immediate pending-capture state. Add a sequencing test that advances the native poll between pointer capture and resolution of `set_pet_dragging(true)`.

- Correct: Aside from the blocker above, no additional blocking findings were verified. Final physical movement is serialized before engine finalization and persistence ([windows/src/window-drag.ts:147](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/window-drag.ts:147)-[155](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/window-drag.ts:155)); the pet host persists before releasing its active lease ([windows/src/pet-window.ts:354](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/pet-window.ts:354)-[360](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/pet-window.ts:360)); manual sampling records the initial and successful physical moves in logical coordinates ([windows/src/roam/engine.ts:235](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/roam/engine.ts:235)-[249](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/roam/engine.ts:249)); and cache generation guards cover stale read/move/scale completions ([windows/src/roam/window.ts:24](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/roam/window.ts:24)-[48](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/roam/window.ts:48), [windows/src/roam/window.ts:93](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/roam/window.ts:93)-[123](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src/roam/window.ts:123)). Tauri `core:window:default` provides the required read/listen/cursor APIs, while explicit set-position/size/focus permissions remain present ([windows/src-tauri/capabilities/default.json:5](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src-tauri/capabilities/default.json:5)-[16](C:/sudy/github/DesktopPet/windows/src-tauri/capabilities/default.json:16)).

